>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Mirsky</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acetylation and methylation of histones and their possible role in the regulation of RNA synthesis</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1964</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>786</fpage><lpage>794</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14172992</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aparicio</surname><given-names>OM</given-names></name><name><surname>Billington</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Gottschling</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modifiers of position effect are shared between telomeric and silent mating-type loci in S. cerevisiae. Cell</article-title><year>1991</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>1279</fpage><lpage>1287</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aravind</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Iyer</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The SWIRM domain: a conserved module found in chromosomal proteins points to novel chromatin-modifying activities</article-title><source>Genome Biol</source><year>2002</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>R39.1</fpage><lpage>R39.7</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Astrom</surname><given-names>SU</given-names></name><name><surname>Cline</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name><name><surname>Rine</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The <italic>Drosophila melanogaster</italic> sir2+ gene is nonessential and has only minor effects on position-effect variegation</article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>2003</year><volume>163</volume><fpage>931</fpage><lpage>937